event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":86,"item_id":"rs_06e36e9afe25538d016ac9e4320294819498bbd5b1aada316a","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Evaluating SSR forms implementation**\n\nI'm thinking about implementing SSR forms for fetch requests. A vanilla form POST redirect would be good for accessibility, utilizing a 400 response to re-render a list. I'll make navigation possible via buttons, using form GET requests for projects by ID, and I don't need any frontend JavaScript. I'll ensure the server has robust routing and a clean environment for integration testing. Also, IDs will be integers with autoincrement."}

