data: {"type":"response.completed","sequence_number":1771,"safety_buffering":false,"response":{"id":"resp_06e36e9afe25538d016ac9e430cc008194940d9cdf46b70edd","object":"response","created_at":1791616048,"completed_at":1791616088,"status":"completed","background":false,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"presence_penalty":0.0,"moderation":null,"model":"gpt-6.1-sol","access_programs":{"cyber":"standard"},"previous_response_id":null,"instructions":"You are an expert coding assistant operating inside pi, a coding agent harness. You help users by reading files, executing commands, editing code, and writing new files.\n\n<tools>\n- read: Read file contents\n- bash: Execute bash commands (ls, grep, find, etc.)\n- edit: Make precise file edits with exact text replacement, including multiple disjoint edits in one call\n- write: Create or overwrite files\n\nIn addition to the tools above, you may have access to other custom tools depending on the project.\n</tools>\n\n<rules>\n- Use bash for file operations like ls, rg, find\n- Use read to examine files instead of cat or sed.\n- You can inspect PI_* environment variables for current model and session details.\n- Use edit for precise changes (edits[].oldText must match exactly)\n- When changing multiple separate locations in one file, use one edit call with multiple entries in edits[] instead of multiple edit calls\n- Each edits[].oldText is matched against the original file, not after earlier edits are applied. Do not emit overlapping or nested edits. Merge nearby changes into one edit.\n- Keep edits[].oldText as small as possible while still being unique in the file. Do not pad with large unchanged regions.\n- Use write only for new files or complete rewrites.\n- Be concise in your responses\n- Show file paths clearly when working with files\n</rules>\n\n<docs>\nPi documentation (read only when the user asks about pi itself, its SDK, extensions, themes, skills, or TUI):\n- Main documentation: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/README.md\n- Additional docs: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs\n- Examples: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/examples (extensions, custom tools, SDK)\n- When reading pi docs or examples, resolve docs/... under Additional docs and examples/... under Examples, not the current working directory\n- When asked about: extensions (docs/extensions.md, examples/extensions/), themes (docs/themes.md), skills (docs/skills.md), prompt templates (docs/prompt-templates.md), TUI components (docs/tui.md), keybindings (docs/keybindings.md), SDK integrations (docs/sdk.md), custom providers (docs/custom-provider.md), adding models (docs/models.md), pi packages (docs/packages.md), environment variables (docs/environment-variables.md), MCP servers (docs/mcp.md), codemode scripts and non-LLM models such as classifiers and image models (docs/codemode.md)\n- When working on pi topics, read the docs and examples, and follow .md cross-references before implementing\n- Always read pi .md files completely and follow links to related docs (e.g., tui.md for TUI API details)\n</docs>\n\n<addendum>\nKeep changes focused and readable. Use clear names and avoid needless duplication. Verify the changed behavior with appropriate checks before submitting.\n</addendum>\n\n<cwd>\n/home/agent/work\n</cwd>","output":[{"type":"reasoning","id":"rs_06e36e9afe25538d016ac9e4320294819498bbd5b1aada316a","summary":[{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Evaluating SSR forms implementation**\n\nI'm thinking about implementing SSR forms for fetch requests. A vanilla form POST redirect would be good for accessibility, utilizing a 400 response to re-render a list. I'll make navigation possible via buttons, using form GET requests for projects by ID, and I don't need any frontend JavaScript. I'll ensure the server has robust routing and a clean environment for integration testing. Also, IDs will be integers with autoincrement."}],"content":[],"encrypted_content":"gAAAAABqyeQ2O9DUJFQHRiuWHG4-vXXln4lR6cukEPgJbBJFgRoAIos__PLqhAAnViI3CP6k2kQhm8YNOs9j4vo_l9M8n-I8W7t4SpkAOhTBXa4zgK_vbQO8kEc0CCWs1_nFbe_2TLf_kZHdRCWbwBL3y7jG0yAhKpvr7YwxbJ14wzEKE6-oJJWjBSgC2dcEBr7GTyRsyMOTmYvX-M47R5L1bB9eyqkP_aS7g0cqiFrs_gy4UB4nCGYf5_6AKYEBYfAuV4KlEBLjSIub2_jokeWFDDLjkPf9h4fpedJ7YjYIb4RUja4rR3rEeJsWJzaoZlmWeJ-XgRbFBZFCmD0zhdnbMcmFtzQDvuwych7l2dZzmszHItSv_Gz2MhAmfHegEBJ7losYXpXMGrv7EkqfXvOfY4_Sp5ngJ1Qh92w9UhFbuakOPvl7hwQzoxXnFq4jZXLed_5rH_YvCjXH3dMh-pbicw-E7E2RShCsaZdeUhuPn9Hw63SqGXvztLxOej1ttIZA3slAOYbt3QPjVlDV80xy_o2xPFGZHQFduRLSxi2LOzD3Hr810Krh-K-C0m3f84-eNgUCu6hgJyolZKmnCJOYEpM9x4CN9byIQTXAzjvWj2ikN6gGffQ7_w470OYNw8dI6xc6iQ0ijSiYyRBJspCoBaFzJQo4TeUoqfkRzJvWl399ddnYiTwDXksPCFeeC8KsL0Jp9VmdqDX-ZM5Toi6Mc0PSLAAKwgtcNYl2TyX4A5lhIAqoJ3CyIpx1Ytu42v1qCqJz7VSMlJrZqb1kkTFQY3ldKP4D6dTbg9BIB4Ou5zAoJeKf0akAi594H_3sBB7gIJMP7fxCKiTpNDZiw0LABPKgYymSHsNMdeR71I9BoHqUkOkyQdOxDWHeDOi45IMwc1sL9b2huFetuGyyI9U9EjOv9NhNUTpNrHlTzjU6eAimgLyz_NuBxm-77qkCTG6TUzyn6tVCTtuGhWiYJes-aEicvPTtN8wRHxKG6Q8nhgANcJVY1BmtmkaH2m3SvCOFaZKta--8ZJ1p9CvSLq50LyifKbyLSG69B1uFW9O-Vx9CvllHIqZZLnI59obsEzOO7c_Q-uoMz7BKFzy7MOZeYrJu0Qt5PWSIG3Ao1F1cexjCgXew6Jjm_8HD9RzHl1m8iPhm2YsMWZ0fR10Gj8Z5pPdiBAG9j-toFZ2lt0QQR1m4sVn6ApgbzN7Jr-g-xsmieRfFT9S_ul3EojjhPJ3BNDTuJk9Fs4nGy74v7sgjstaZsuomtCmziG0QVFvCjaZjiD1wxiD7624TMHkmNO3gFXLkCWyyU1sgYvfG0Vsquq-uu8xk2A-uTVFRzLmP4Ug_OoOA4a32wZfzeUaLcsW5Lxvkr9Bx9PDkVc7cGqYOlIP76z0wV4TDeCW1eTgRAwipsKrRBHZ0Lca0dmz0tn7XP2LBqE1XB4jns1pnTZy1vqFjn2Ofuh6ZNRaGNuSEqZefeKX7yV6P62l8Jzp4Uh0bfdioSbPHI72RRHeL_Dap6T1TDGUG43FOpGvP6f6PLKXwtkBwarsGvxqXpqCn6SPsVZBlPiaiQcLDoi5OVQaqwtBT9BCtjeTmPtwrq_lC3-GL6nYwcKznRHOGVAflc8HMhV25jrj0X6tih5MpNU0OgippdjertU-IHdCU_mcUCiJN7lxNMeAaagiwWsw7YAUPVE0dtkP3dZwoa_XT3X6xhzcHGxaNgJJAgPFbb33ji2GLmOElDId2kyQCCvz47Ea1WOyfLuotonqkhxd5GVXQtDqBOAcQAb834_zzvVYtMoh1Sa8dkURX8uio4NHzo5UJJ4q9tB5lt5lN7wSkLg0TZLblBE-rO6Zica1n_6CBSHIG96rTMmuwdzPB2uedwILJcNmn4P8X49rSOKkF1iWJgGTwCx9q4PdpkBWUU6LeQS0-53mNru4weWZoP